---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
const updated = "4 November 2026";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="SuperFlyer — Privacy Policy"
  description="Privacy policy for SuperFlyer, the comic and flyer app by DataIsland Software LLC."
>

  <section class="legal fade-in">
    <div class="breadcrumb"><a href="/privacy">← All Privacy Policies</a></div>

    <h1>SuperFlyer — Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="meta">DataIsland Software LLC &nbsp;·&nbsp; Last updated: {updated}</p>

    <p>
      SuperFlyer is an app for making comics, flyers and picture stories on the Mac. This policy
      explains what SuperFlyer does with your information.
    </p>

    <h2>Summary</h2>
    <p>
      <strong>SuperFlyer does not collect personal data.</strong> It has no account, no analytics
      and no advertising. Your comics are files on your Mac. DataIsland never receives your comics,
      pictures, words or prompts.
    </p>

    <h2>Your Comics</h2>
    <p>
      Comics are saved as files where you choose, with their pictures and clips inside. They are
      not uploaded anywhere by SuperFlyer. If you keep them in iCloud Drive, Apple's iCloud terms apply.
    </p>

    <h2>Features That Run on Your Mac</h2>
    <p>
      Image Playground drawings, Apple Intelligence writing help, translation (Translate Book),
      Cut Out Subject and the comic looks all run on your Mac using Apple's frameworks. Apple's own
      privacy policy covers Image Playground and Apple Intelligence; when Apple Intelligence uses
      Private Cloud Compute, Apple processes that request under its privacy commitments.
    </p>

    <h2>Optional Cloud AI (OpenRouter)</h2>
    <p>
      If you choose to add your own OpenRouter API key, the "Draw with OpenRouter", "Animate" and
      "Make with AI" features send your prompt, and any reference pictures you've chosen, from your
      Mac directly to OpenRouter and the AI model you select. That traffic does not pass through
      DataIsland. OpenRouter's and the model provider's privacy policies apply. Your key is stored
      in your Mac's keychain. These features are off unless you add a key. New Classroom Comic switches off all AI tools
      for that comic, including the ones that run on your Mac.
    </p>
    <p>
      Pictures made this way are marked as AI-generated inside the comic ("How this was made"),
      and flip-books that include them say so.
    </p>

    <h2>Photos and Files</h2>
    <p>
      SuperFlyer only sees the photos and files you pick. Photos you choose are copied into your
      comic. SuperFlyer does not read the rest of your Photos library.
    </p>

    <h2>Flip-Books You Publish</h2>
    <p>
      A flip-book is a folder of web files you export. If you put it online, it's hosted by the
      service you choose and anyone with the link can read it. Flip-books contain no tracking code.
      Tip Jar buttons link to the web addresses you type in.
    </p>

    <h2>Crash Reports</h2>
    <p>
      If you've agreed to share analytics with app developers in macOS settings, Apple may send
      DataIsland anonymous crash and performance reports through the App Store. They contain no
      personal information or comic content.
    </p>

    <h2>Children</h2>
    <p>
      SuperFlyer collects no personal data from anyone, including children. Teachers can use
      New Classroom Comic, which switches off all AI tools for that comic.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Questions about this policy: <a href="mailto:support@dataisland.com">support@dataisland.com</a>.
    </p>
  </section>

</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .legal {
    max-width: 800px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 3rem 0 5rem;
    border-bottom: none;
  }

  .breadcrumb { margin-bottom: 2rem; font-size: 0.9rem; }
  .legal h1 { font-size: 2.1rem; margin-bottom: 0.5rem; }
  .meta { font-size: 0.9rem; color: var(--gray); margin-bottom: 2rem; }
  .legal h2 { margin-top: 2.25rem; margin-bottom: 0.6rem; font-size: 1.2rem; }
  .legal h3 { margin-top: 1.5rem; margin-bottom: 0.5rem; font-size: 1rem; font-weight: 600; }
  .legal p  { font-size: 1rem; line-height: 1.7; margin-bottom: 0.9rem; }

  ul { margin: 0.5rem 0 1rem 1.25rem; color: var(--gray-dark); }
  ul li { margin-bottom: 0.4rem; font-size: 0.97rem; line-height: 1.5; }
</style>
